# Line endings for the setup scripts. Scoped narrowly on purpose -- a blanket
# "* text=auto" would renormalize every existing file and bury real changes in a
# whole-repo whitespace diff.
#
# The .sh entry is the load-bearing one: cloned on Windows without it, git would
# hand out CRLF and the shebang becomes "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r", which fails as
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" -- an error that names a file that
# plainly exists, so it reads as a broken script rather than a checkout setting.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
